A: Split picker (recommended). Searchable list beside a persistent selected tray. The recipient, selection, card approval note, and final action stay in view. On mobile, Selected switches the main list to the chosen set.

B: Side drawer. A compact picker stays over the vault. It keeps page context, with less room for account details and no simultaneous selected tray.

C: Choose, then review. A dedicated page shows the picker, then a separate recipient and selected-credentials review screen. More room and a deliberate confirmation step, with an extra click.

Shared behavior:
- One Invite to vault entry point for logins, API keys, and cards.
- 30 sample items: 18 logins, 8 API keys, 4 cards.
- Search by name, account, or website; type filters; Selected view.
- Select all current results or remove all current results. These actions affect saved items matching the current view only.
- Selection persists across search and type filters; lists and trays scroll within bounded areas; the final action remains visible.
- New invitations start empty. The canvas mocks show four selected midway through the flow.
- Future saved credentials stay private.
- Each card purchase requires owner approval.
- A different recipient clears the draft selection.
- Prototype Invite only shows a preview. It grants no actual access.

These designs do not establish runtime authorization or prove the reported Gmail isolation issue is fixed.
`}));
